Because of the cursing problem in the late game I do not like to use the
samurai Quest weapon. Samurai are already nearly guaranteed both
Excalibur and Snickersnee both of which are ascendable melee weapons.
With a samurai I'll pick a secondary weapon that's not a short sword
and run up the skills.

Because samurai can get expert in bow I tend to wait until maxxed out
luck and ability to bless big stacks of arrows before I enhance that
slot past skilled but once I do I'll push it to expert.  Machine gun
fired d4 ya is better than any two-handed weapon. With a samurai I
tend to alternate between wielding the bow firing arrows and two-hand
wielding either Ex or Snick and a dagger in the early game, saber in
the mid-game and one.  Or an elven broadsword as the secondary wield if
no saber presents itself in the game.  Sometimes it's Greyswandir and a
long sword.

For samurai I like to keep moving up XP levels because it is nice to be
expert in three skill schools.

The order goes something like, dagger to basic (max), long sword to
skilled, two weapon to basic, two weapon to skilled, bow to skilled,
saber to basic (max), bow to expert (max), long sword to expert (max),
two weapon to expert (max), with spells, polearms or other items mixed
in as appropriate.


